One small note. Therea re actually 2 system prompts responsible for GroupChat. One is the usual system message at the top of the conversation, and the other is added at the end of the conversation right as we prompt the LLM to make a decision. In responding to your earlier comments, I extracted the floating system prompt to a separate function to facilitate subclassing. But because there are two functions to replace, and they have to be coordinated and work together, I opted to the subclassing approach for now. I'd be happy to consider alternatives (e.g., speaker selection), but it would be slightly complex.

@IANTHEREAL This PR adds only marginal improvements to GroupChat as-is (GAIA level 1 scores move from 20% to 25%), but separating the description from the system prompt is the basis for a bunch of further improvements and experimentation I have planned.

There are *many* concerns with group chat, but the description field is the basis for many solutions.

I would be happy to remove my contrib GroupChatModerator class if we can just get the description field added to main!

